From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:23:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ACCOUNTS-1: keep the instalment when a flat-rate loan is
 prepaid by reducing the tenure

keepInstalment priced the months a kept instalment needs as a reducing
balance loan, even for a flat one. 2,40,000 at 15% flat over 24 months is
13,000 a month (10,000 principal + 3,000 interest on the original
principal). After 12 instalments, 30,000 prepaid leaves 90,000: kept at
13,000 that is 90,000 / 10,000 = 9 more, tenure 21. Reducing balance gave
8, tenure 20, and the flat schedule then asked 90,000 / 8 + 3,000 = 14,250
-- "reduce the tenure" raised the instalment by 1,250.

A flat loan's months are now the outstanding over the principal part of the
kept instalment, rounded up so no instalment exceeds it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
